+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+Every tool declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is handed verbatim to the providers, and `ToolRegistry.execute` checks the model's input against that schema before the executor runs. Input the schema rejects is answered with a `ToolResponse` the model can read and correct within the tool-round budget, rather than a throw that ends the conversation; only an unknown tool name still throws.
+
+## Contract
+
+- Input missing a `required` property is answered with a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property, and the executor is never invoked ([validated by: returns a rejection naming the missing required property and never runs the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L34)).
+- A rejection names the failing property path and the constraint that failed, and neither the returned `result` nor any log line contains a property value from the rejected input ([validated by: names the failing path and expected type but never the offending value, in the result or the logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L47)).
+- A static tool's schema is compiled at `register` time, so an uncompilable schema throws there with a message naming the tool ([validated by: throws at register time for an uncompilable schema, naming the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L68)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` is validated against the schema it returns for that call, not one cached from an earlier call ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema current at each call, not a stale one](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L79)).
+- In the orchestrator's tool loop a rejected call does not reject `processMessage`: the rejection text reaches the provider as the tool result on the next round, and a corrected retry runs the executor ([validated by: resolves, shows the rejection to the provider on the next round, and runs the corrected retry](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L106)).
